## What Color Base Works Best for Leopard Print Nails on Your Skin Tone

Warm undertones look best in caramel, honey, and terracotta leopard bases. Cool undertones look sharper in ash beige, true black and white, or icy taupe. Neutral undertones can wear almost any base, including bold color, without the print fighting the skin.

The quickest way to check your undertone doesn't require a chart. Look at the veins on the inside of your wrist in daylight. Blue or purple reads cool. Green reads warm. A mix of both, or veins that don't clearly lean either way, reads neutral. Gold jewelry sitting better than silver is another warm signal, and the reverse points cool. Once you know where you land, the base color decision practically makes itself, and that's before you've even chosen a spot pattern.

