## Classic Leopard Print Nails Done Right

Most people assume classic leopard print means loud, and that assumption is exactly backwards. A well-placed rosette on a soft nude base is one of the most restrained manicures in the maximalist category, precisely because the print does the talking and the color stays quiet.

The formula holds across nail lengths and shapes: two to three tonal spots per rosette, a darker brown or black outline, and enough negative space between clusters that the print reads as pattern rather than clutter. Overcrowd the spots and it tips into costume territory fast. Space them with intention and it reads expensive.

