## Leopard French Tips for a Subtler Take

Is leopard print too much for someone who has never worn an animal print manicure before? Not when it's confined to the tip.

A leopard French tip replaces the classic white edge with a strip of rosette pattern, and keeps the rest of the nail a plain nude or sheer base. That's the whole definition: the print lives only at the tip, the body of the nail stays clean, and the result reads as a French manicure with one confident twist rather than a full leopard set. It's the version that made the trend recognisable outside beauty circles in the first place, largely thanks to Hailey Bieber's leopard French tip mani and Vanessa Hudgens's take on the same idea finished with a glassy cat-eye topcoat.

