## Leopard Print Accent Nails If You Want Just a Hint

One nail. That's the entire commitment level of an accent approach, and it's the lowest-risk way into the print.

Paint every nail a solid neutral, then reserve the ring finger, or the thumb, for the full rosette pattern. The rest of the set stays calm, the accent nail carries the entire personality of the manicure, and the whole thing takes barely longer than a plain manicure to apply. It's a smart entry point if you've been curious about **leopard print nails** but weren't ready to wear the pattern across all ten fingers.

