## Reverse Leopard Print and Negative Space Designs

Most people picture leopard print as spots on a solid base. Reverse leopard print flips that entirely.

A reverse take on **leopard print nails** places the rosette outlines on a sheer, clear, or negative-space base instead of a solid color underneath. The spots become the only pigment on the nail, floating against bare or barely-there polish, which gives the whole design a lighter, more architectural feel than a full-coverage set. It's one of the newest ways to wear the print, and it solves the "is this too much" hesitation some readers have without losing the pattern entirely.

