## Leopard Print Mixed With Other Trends

Does leopard print actually pair with anything beyond itself? It layers into nearly every trend currently circulating without losing its identity.

Cherries scattered over one or two nails alongside a leopard base give the set a playful, slightly retro edge. Florals dropped in as a single accent soften the print's intensity. Cat-eye gel finishes, the same one Vanessa Hudgens wore over her leopard French tips, add a magnetic shimmer that changes how the spots catch light depending on the angle. None of these combinations require abandoning the leopard base. They just add one more layer of texture on top of it.

