## Matte vs Glossy: Which Finish Suits Leopard Print

Matte wins for everyday wear and a quieter, velvet-like read. Glossy wins when the goal is shine and maximum print definition.

A matte topcoat softens the contrast between the base and the spots, giving the whole design a slightly blurred, textural finish that photographs beautifully but reads calmer in person, closer to actual fur than painted pattern. Glossy does the opposite: it sharpens every rosette edge and makes the spots pop against the base with more contrast, which suits the design when the print itself is meant to be the focal point rather than a texture.

